## 3. Form Component Structure

### 3.1 File Organization
Place form-related code in route's structure:

```
src/app/mypage/
  components/
    create-invitation-form.tsx  # Form UI component
  api/
    schemas.ts                  # Zod schemas
    actions.server.ts           # Server Actions
  types/
    index.ts                    # Type exports (if needed)
```

### 3.2 Form Component Rules
- Form components must be Client Components (`"use client"`)
- Use `react-hook-form` for form state management
- Use `zodResolver` for validation
- Call Server Actions on submit
- Handle errors and show user feedback

---

## 4. shadcn/ui Component Usage

### 4.1 Preferred Components
Use shadcn/ui components for:
- Forms: `Form`, `FormField`, `FormItem`, `FormLabel`, `FormControl`, `FormMessage`
- Inputs: `Input`, `Textarea`, `Select`, `Checkbox`, `RadioGroup`
- Buttons: `Button` (with variants: default, destructive, outline, secondary, ghost, link)
- Feedback: `Toast`, `Alert`, `Dialog`
- Layout: `Card`, `Separator`, `Tabs`

### 4.2 Component Variants
Use built-in variants for consistency:

```typescript
<Button variant="default" size="default">Submit</Button>
<Button variant="destructive" size="sm">Delete</Button>
<Button variant="outline" size="lg">Cancel</Button>
```

### 4.3 Customization
- Customize via CSS variables in `globals.css`
- Extend components in `src/components/ui/` when needed
- Maintain accessibility (ARIA attributes are handled by shadcn/ui)

---

## 5. Error Handling Patterns

### 5.1 Field-Level Errors
Display field errors using `FormMessage`:

```typescript
<FormField
  control={form.control}
  name="email"
  render={({ field }) => (
    <FormItem>
      <FormLabel>이메일</FormLabel>
      <FormControl>
        <Input type="email" {...field} />
      </FormControl>
      <FormMessage /> {/* Automatically shows field errors */}
    </FormItem>
  )}
/>
```

### 5.2 Form-Level Errors
Show form-level errors with Toast or Alert:

```typescript
if (!result.ok && !result.error.fieldErrors) {
  toast({
    variant: "destructive",
    title: "오류",
    description: result.error.message,
  });
}
```

### 5.3 Server Action Error Response
Server Actions must return structured errors:

```typescript
{
  ok: false,
  error: {
    code: "VALIDATION_ERROR" | "UNAUTHORIZED" | "NOT_FOUND" | "CONFLICT" | "INTERNAL_ERROR",
    message: string,
    fieldErrors?: Record<string, string[]>, // For validation errors
  }
}
```

